Revision history for Data-Coloured

{{$NEXT}}
  - A multi-byte UTF-8 character is now rendered from its UTF-8 bytes instead
    of its code point, so "ä" shows up as <c3a4> and not as <e4>.
  - The distribution builds from the source tree and ships the Perl 5 licence
    as a committed LICENSE file.
  - README.md documents the module, its two export tiers and all four functions.
  - Continuous integration runs on GitHub Actions for Perl 5.36, 5.38 and 5.40.
  - Declare the runtime dependencies Term::ANSIColor and Exporter in the
    cpanfile, so the distribution installs its dependencies automatically.
  - DDC exports all four functions coloured, poloured, pc and c, so a script
    that imports DDC gets the complete API of Data::Coloured.
  - The ddc script shows its usage for --help and -h on STDOUT, reports an
    unknown option, a missing file and a closed standard input on STDERR
    and exits with 2, 1 and 1, so a broken command line is told apart from
    a successful run.
  - The ddc script points its SUPPORT section at the repository of this
    distribution.
